(THG2-67: a field default must be a literal of the field's own type. A float
 literal on a number field is refused, and the message names both types. The
 documented exception - a whole number is accepted for a float - was run by
 hand: `a float called weight is 2.` compiles and prints {weight: 2.0}. The
 mismatch check misfires on an unsupported field type; see Discrepancy 4.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox THG2-67.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   error: Field 'x' of thing 'point' is a number, but its default is a float
   followed by "A field's default must be a literal of the field's own type; a
   whole number is accepted for a float." No binary is produced; this is a
   compile error.
)
